1
00:00:01,860 --> 00:00:02,800
Lesson One.

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:07,440
An old man and a baby are stranded on
an island full of deadly predators.

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,837
You sail to the island to save them,

4
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:13,437
but only one person other than
you can fit on your rescue boat.

5
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,880
What are you gonna do?

6
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:17,850
Umm...

7
00:00:17,933 --> 00:00:19,440
Oh, I get it! Okay!

8
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:21,537
I'll get off the boat and stay there!

9
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:23,497
Then the baby AND old man will fit!

10
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:24,637
That would save the boat!

11
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:25,880
No, idiot!

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,177
Wrong answer!

13
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:32,960
The old geezer's gonna die soon, anyway!

14
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:35,540
So abandon him!

15
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:37,250
Wado?

16
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:39,379
Vice Admiral, don't tell them that!

17
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:40,740
Think hard.

18
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:43,660
Why are you boys here in the first place?

19
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:47,360
Why did you join the Navy?

20
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:51,139
There's something out there
worth protecting, right?

21
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:53,300
So what is it?

22
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:58,277
All of us, all of us, dream, save us?

23
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:03,037
All of us, all of us!

24
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:33,700
of

25
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:47,740
us.

26
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:14,380
I love you.

27
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,057
those indentations there?

28
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:54,140
Those are fist marks from someone
using the armor of the warships as

29
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:55,150
punching bags.

30
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:56,440
Punching bags?

31
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:57,917
Do you know who did it?

32
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,140
Vice Admiral Garb,
starting when he was young.

33
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:03,400
He's kept it up for decades now.

34
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:04,600
It's his routine.

35
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:05,877
He's still doing it?

36
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:07,489
Why are there two of them?

37
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:13,177
The other belonged to Garb's
protege, the former admiral, Aokiji.

38
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:16,200
You can't use Haki or
devil through powers.

39
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:18,397
That's the rule of battleship bagging.

40
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:20,598
This is the strength of a true hero.

41
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,676
It's not something you're bored with.

42
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:50,900
And put set of flying straight to the sea!

43
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,339
Don't you monster!

44
00:03:59,080 --> 00:03:59,910
Quick!

45
00:03:59,993 --> 00:04:01,937
We gotta pull him out or he's gonna drown!

46
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:04,373
How the hell are we supposed to do that?

47
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:08,700
He beat the boss in one shot!

48
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:10,272
He can't fight this guy!

49
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:12,520
Thank you so much, Vice Admiral.

50
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:14,820
That's the legendary hero for you.

51
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:17,733
Save it, boys, I'm just getting started!

52
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:23,880
Legendary hero, my ass!

53
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:29,100
You're nothing but an old hat
who's been trashing a hideout!

54
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:32,680
And now we're gonna make
you pay for the damages!

55
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:41,680
Drive and spread fire!

56
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:52,940
Pirate! Fireballs!

57
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:07,580
Ouch! That's odd!

58
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,040
Stop burning me!

59
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:19,917
Are you trying to sink all island?

60
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,657
Calm down, you maniac!

61
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:25,117
What are we gonna do when
Commodore Teach comes back?

62
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:28,017
If he sees his face like
this, he'll kill us all!

63
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:33,617
We got garb,

64
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:35,317
outnumbered and he doesn't even flinch!

65
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:36,757
What's wrong with him?

66
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:42,037
We're in the clear!

67
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:44,377
Vice Admiral, the prisoners, our soldiers?

68
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:47,037
and all the injured have been
evacuated from the island.

69
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,717
They're all aboard the ship now.

70
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,220
Good, nice work.

71
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:52,480
Hibari, stay strong!

72
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,540
Watch the frozen ones, fold them slowly.

73
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:59,460
Captain, Koby, please be safe.

74
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:01,679
We're ready to set off at any time.

75
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:05,100
Okay, we're all done here, pull back!

76
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:07,940
Koby, Hababu, Bruce, come on!

77
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:10,110
Right!

78
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,920
On my way!

79
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:17,480
I won't miss this
hellhole, that's for sure!

80
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:21,637
This place sure lives up to the talk.

81
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:26,191
You poke a hole anywhere and these damn
pirates swarm out one after another!

82
00:06:34,940 --> 00:06:38,700
I'm sorry, Garb, but like I
said, I can't let you leave.

83
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:40,260
Get ready.

84
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,937
I should have run, but
I still had the chance!

85
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:45,840
Oh, jeez. I'm dead.

86
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:48,946
Before we fight, I'm
your favorite too, right?

87
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:51,760
You sure you want to do this, Kuzan?

88
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:55,720
All of Blackbeard's officers
are dangerous. Be careful.

89
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,200
We don't have to beat them.

90
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:02,284
All we got to do is drag
our asses to the coast.

91
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,820
Don't let them kill you.

92
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:06,530
Yes, sir!

93
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:15,360
Somebody help me! Oh no!

94
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:17,737
I must have left one of
the prisoners behind!

95
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:19,160
I'm on my way, ma 'am!

96
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:22,317
Thank goodness we didn't
set sail without her!

97
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,780
Kobe, wait! Don't go!

98
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:25,140
It's a trap!

99
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:45,240
Vice Admiral Garp

100
00:07:57,940 --> 00:07:58,900
Bastard!

101
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:03,920
What?

102
00:08:04,180 --> 00:08:05,457
Was he invisible somehow?

103
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:06,780
Oh, sure to you.

104
00:08:07,220 --> 00:08:10,280
I think Empel Down was
a better fit for you.

105
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:21,180
Whoa! Get him! Got him!

106
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:24,320
Get rid of that sword
straight through Wired Guard!

107
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:28,100
You okay, Garp?

108
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:29,860
I'll be fine!

109
00:08:30,060 --> 00:08:31,589
Just get back on the ship!

110
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:39,417
This is all my fault he
got hurt defending me don't

111
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:43,080
flatter yourself Koby I
was his target all along.

112
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:56,977
Don't give up easy do you old
man it looks like garps worn

113
00:08:57,060 --> 00:09:00,295
down you see any who was just
waiting to make his move?

114
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,900
Even normal guys like us
can take him down now.

115
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:05,910
Let's go!

116
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:12,600
All we gotta do is finish the old man off
and we'll be set for life! Hurry! Hurry!

117
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,877
Drop is worth as much as an animal!

118
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,842
He's got a free crown dowdy hat!

119
00:09:16,980 --> 00:09:18,980
That's like three billion berries!

120
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:38,360
It's Kuzan!

121
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,320
Out of my way, Smallfrize!

122
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:50,660
Even if his hands and feet were tied
together, you still couldn't kill Garp!

123
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:53,460
Leave this to me!

124
00:09:58,520 --> 00:09:59,800
Ice claw!

125
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:09,620
Hey, Garp.

126
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:15,640
I want you to mentor me.

127
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:19,280
Are you being serious?

128
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:22,280
Nah, I like my freedom.

129
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:24,345
Go bother one of the trainers.

130
00:10:24,860 --> 00:10:26,457
They've taught me all they can.

131
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:27,658
I'm ready for more.

132
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:29,120
Please teach me.

133
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:30,400
I said no!

134
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:31,780
Get lost!

135
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:47,950
Ow!

136
00:10:48,033 --> 00:10:48,863
Damn, that hurts.

137
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:53,837
You better not use Haki.

138
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:55,449
That won't help you learn.

139
00:10:56,260 --> 00:10:58,436
I don't even know how to do that yet.

140
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:04,440
Let's do this!

141
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,520
What is justice to the Navy?

142
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:45,980
I don't even know anymore.

143
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:48,880
Not after a lot of time.

144
00:11:53,900 --> 00:11:56,280
My son became a revolutionary!

145
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:57,810
Huh?

146
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,120
Damn it!

147
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:13,470
Kuzan!

148
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:15,120
What's wrong with you?

149
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:18,057
My grandson says he wants
to be a damn pirate!

150
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:18,970
What?

151
00:12:19,053 --> 00:12:20,445
Why the hell would he do that?

152
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:22,340
I have no idea.

153
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:24,114
I gotta eat something.

154
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:25,097
Want to join me?

155
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:26,517
I have work to do.

156
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:29,340
Did you forget I'm an admiral? T?

157
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:30,780
Come on.

158
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:40,380
You trained a powerful enemy for yourself.

159
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:43,980
You're expelled, you dunce.

160
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:18,800
Vice-Admiral, no! No!

161
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:23,390
Garp!

162
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:26,380
Got him well after all.

163
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:30,540
Keep him safe, no matter what.

164
00:13:32,220 --> 00:13:35,860
Every second you stay here,
your odds get worse and worse.

165
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:39,580
This is Pirate Island after all.

166
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:42,800
They're gonna keep coming
till you're full of lead.

167
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:47,606
You think I can't sink my claws into that
ship you've got waiting off the coast?

168
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:55,600
Allow me to demyawinstrate
the power of my Ayo-Ayo fruit.

169
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:58,760
Are you alright?

170
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:01,320
Take it slow. You're safe now.

171
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:02,750
Where is Kobe?

172
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:05,700
Please tell me he made it out. I'm sorry.

173
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:07,901
I caused you all so much trouble.

174
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:10,440
He'll be with us soon.

175
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:12,391
And you're never trouble.

176
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:24,950
Captain!

177
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:26,139
We've got trouble!

178
00:14:29,380 --> 00:14:33,620
All you see in the papers is
Blackbeard this and Blackbeard that.

179
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,280
Well, meow, you'll see what I can do.

180
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:41,060
Let me give you a sneak preview
of tomorrow's big news story.

181
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:43,997
The famous Vice Admiral Garp led a team of

182
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:46,997
promising young elites in
an attack on Pirate Island.

183
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:52,140
They attempted to rescue Captain
Koby, the hero of the Navy.

184
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:23,137
But then the fourth ship
captain of the Blackbeard

185
00:15:23,220 --> 00:15:26,580
Pirates struck and they bowed before him.

186
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:32,260
The great Avalo Pizarro
proved far too mighty.

187
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:40,040
And all of those poor brave furries
were completely annihilated.

188
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,680
No, please don't do this.

189
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:49,606
There are civilians on board.

190
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:51,701
Those people aren't your enemies.

191
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:00,677
Calm down, Kobe.

192
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:02,397
Mark my words, boy.

193
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:04,280
Justice will prevail.

194
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:16,920
Let's have some fun.

195
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:21,930
Blockbuster!

196
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:23,160
Don't do this.

197
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:24,560
Please let us go.

198
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:26,857
You're taking us to
Pirate Island, aren't you?

199
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:28,764
What are you going to do to us?

200
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,377
Didn't think Rayleigh would
stick his nose in my business,

201
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:39,077
but I got some nice
souvenirs, so who cares?

202
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:40,080
Zeh!

203
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:44,219
Vice Admiral, they're our comrades.

204
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,618
Can we do anything?

205
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:47,640
We're letting our men down.

206
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:50,080
We need permission from above.

207
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,400
Blackbeard is an emperor.

208
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:54,160
I know, but...

209
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:55,710
Zeh!

210
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:08,457
What is he doing?

211
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:11,422
Vice Admiral, Captain Koby
is with S .W .O .R .D.

212
00:17:11,580 --> 00:17:12,880
S .W .O .R .D., huh?

213
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:17,360
Well, if it isn't Koby the hero, so what?

214
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:20,033
You come here to take your friends back?

215
00:17:20,120 --> 00:17:24,040
If you want to start an Alto
war, that's just P .G. with me.

216
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:29,207
You're capturing 800 marines and also
commandeering one of our warships, right?

217
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:31,080
Let them go!

218
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:33,500
And you can take me instead!

219
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:46,997
You think pretty highly of
yourself, don't you, kid?

220
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:49,397
But your life is worth it.

221
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:51,100
You got a deal!

222
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:57,777
How is this even real?

223
00:17:57,860 --> 00:18:00,197
It's too huge.

224
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:03,580
We can't fight that thing.

225
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:12,540
What is that?!

226
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:17,680
Open fire!

227
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:28,500
It's no use!

228
00:18:28,740 --> 00:18:30,000
It isn't stopping!

229
00:18:30,420 --> 00:18:31,840
We have to pull away!

230
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,460
Move the ship back!

231
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:37,560
Not on my watch!

232
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:43,220
They can still reach us!

233
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:49,960
Oh no!

234
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:55,120
If that hand comes down on them, hundreds
of soldiers and civilians will die!

235
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:56,980
We can't fight it!

236
00:18:57,120 --> 00:18:58,649
Where would we even start?

237
00:18:58,940 --> 00:19:00,860
Call everyone up to the deck!

238
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:02,680
Prepare to abandon ship!

239
00:19:03,020 --> 00:19:04,460
Keep the civilians safe!

240
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:06,280
This is all my fault!

241
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:09,688
Everyone here is going
to die because of me!

242
00:19:13,340 --> 00:19:16,220
I surrendered myself
to protect my comrades.

243
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:19,465
But all I've done is put
more people in danger.

244
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:21,560
I can't protect anyone!

245
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,540
I can't do this!

246
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:40,220
You can do it.

247
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:46,520
You can save them.

248
00:19:49,340 --> 00:19:51,080
Vice Admiral Garp?

249
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:55,920
Stay calm.

250
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:58,640
I've got a plan.

251
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:02,760
I'll create an opening for you.

252
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:10,840
First, Captain Koby, you climb up to that
big rock bastard's hand and destroy it.

253
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:12,310
What?

254
00:20:12,393 --> 00:20:13,820
But how can I do that?

255
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:19,100
Rear Admiral Course, when pieces of the
hand fall down, you protect the ship.

256
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:24,080
Lieutenant Commander Hamapo, don't
let anyone stand in their way.

257
00:20:24,340 --> 00:20:25,540
I can try.

258
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:26,920
Vice Admiral, wait.

259
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:29,097
What if I can't...

260
00:20:29,180 --> 00:20:31,020
Hesitation means defeat.

261
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:32,810
Go!

262
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,020
Yes, sir!

263
00:20:52,340 --> 00:20:54,620
Oh, me and the others are on the move!

264
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:57,320
Give it up!

265
00:20:57,540 --> 00:21:00,900
Without guard, you're all
going straight into the sea!

266
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:04,560
They're coming!

267
00:21:05,020 --> 00:21:08,080
El Meppo, go get them! Huh? Why me?

268
00:21:08,660 --> 00:21:11,380
Because those were your orders! Fine then!

269
00:21:11,580 --> 00:21:12,756
But I don't like it!

270
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,720
Let's see what you've got!

271
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:18,792
That's a little garbage!

272
00:21:20,580 --> 00:21:22,880
Come on, Kobe, what's the plan here?

273
00:21:23,260 --> 00:21:24,977
Do you have a bomb or something?

274
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:26,060
I've got nothing.

275
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:28,637
I'll just have to play it by ear for now.

276
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:29,955
Wait, play it by ear?

277
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:34,177
You can't just play it by ear fighting
something big enough to crush a damn warship.

278
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:35,340
Trust me, I know.

279
00:21:35,620 --> 00:21:37,120
Burn in hell, Kobe!

280
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:40,130
Amit?

281
00:21:43,380 --> 00:21:44,210
Kobe?

282
00:21:44,980 --> 00:21:48,862
Lieutenant Commander Helmepo, don't
let anyone stand in their way.

283
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:50,460
Here I go!

284
00:21:54,540 --> 00:21:55,370
This...

285
00:21:55,453 --> 00:21:56,440
is up to you!

286
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:58,780
Get back!

287
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:02,600
Helmepo, no!

288
00:22:03,020 --> 00:22:05,617
Don't look back! Just go! But I...

289
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:06,960
You have a job to do!

290
00:22:13,600 --> 00:22:16,440
I'd sit back down if I were you, Garp.

291
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:21,340
Keep moving and you'll bleed out.

292
00:22:22,520 --> 00:22:24,460
This is just a scratch.

293
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:31,820
I'm trying to spare your life.

294
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:34,160
Sounds soft to me.

295
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:09,160
What are you doing here?

296
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:12,737
Wait, don't you care
what'll happen to the ship?

297
00:23:12,820 --> 00:23:18,020
Galaxi Divine!

298
00:23:42,940 --> 00:23:44,400
Wait! What happened?

299
00:23:44,740 --> 00:23:45,799
It's pulling back!

300
00:23:48,580 --> 00:23:50,380
So this is your opening, huh?

301
00:23:50,660 --> 00:23:51,700
The arm went up.

302
00:23:52,020 --> 00:23:53,320
What now, Kobe?

303
00:23:58,360 --> 00:23:59,760
Okay, here I go!

304
00:24:02,420 --> 00:24:03,250
Kobe!

305
00:24:08,580 --> 00:24:10,860
Oh, now you've done it.

306
00:24:14,780 --> 00:24:18,520
You think that's enough to stop me? Ha!

307
00:24:18,940 --> 00:24:20,457
I'll make you pay!

308
00:24:20,540 --> 00:24:23,540
Stand back and watch me do this!

309
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:27,500
I'll send your men to their graves!

310
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:32,940
And there's nothing you can do
about it! It's back! Take cover!

311
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:36,900
You can cry all you like,
but we've already won!

312
00:24:39,660 --> 00:24:44,800
Hey, Almepo, Coby's making good progress,
but why the hell's he always injured?

313
00:24:45,380 --> 00:24:46,560
You noticed, huh?

314
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:51,320
Oh, well, he said not to tell
you, but I guess I better.

315
00:24:59,940 --> 00:25:04,777
I can't fight as well as everyone else,
even if I train ten times as much as him.

316
00:25:04,860 --> 00:25:08,400
So I'll train a hundred, no,
two hundred times harder.

317
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:14,020
If that's what it takes to be a proper
marine to help people, then I'll do it!

318
00:25:22,180 --> 00:25:23,200
That's enough!

319
00:25:23,540 --> 00:25:24,637
Don't be stupid!

320
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:26,680
You're gonna destroy yourself!

321
00:25:27,380 --> 00:25:31,797
You're telling me he's been training
by himself on top of my drills?

322
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:33,020
Yes, sir.

323
00:25:33,260 --> 00:25:37,380
He's been punching the battleship
back every single night.

324
00:25:44,120 --> 00:25:48,500
And he comes back with his
fists covered in blood.

325
00:25:58,620 --> 00:25:59,457
Faster!

326
00:25:59,540 --> 00:26:00,720
Go faster!

327
00:26:01,880 --> 00:26:03,760
I HAVE TO MAKE IT IN TIME!

328
00:26:11,840 --> 00:26:12,800
Is that...

329
00:26:14,780 --> 00:26:15,610
Help me!

330
00:26:17,520 --> 00:26:18,820
What are you doing?

331
00:26:20,620 --> 00:26:22,240
Hold on, that's Koby!

332
00:26:22,600 --> 00:26:24,677
Is he really trying to stop that ant?

333
00:26:24,760 --> 00:26:26,220
He's gonna get crushed!

334
00:26:26,420 --> 00:26:28,357
I know they call him a hero, but look!

335
00:26:28,440 --> 00:26:32,020
Next to Pisano, the kid is
like the size of an ant.

336
00:26:32,360 --> 00:26:33,380
Kobe, why?

337
00:26:33,760 --> 00:26:35,160
Just protect yourself.

338
00:26:35,380 --> 00:26:38,020
Don't worry about us. Get away. Go back.

339
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:41,280
Hey, Kobe.

340
00:26:41,660 --> 00:26:42,660
You made it.

341
00:26:43,100 --> 00:26:46,512
You got a front row seat to
the death of all your friends.

342
00:26:46,660 --> 00:26:50,860
Even if they dive into the sea,
Aokiji will freeze them solid.

343
00:26:52,880 --> 00:26:55,420
Time to take out the kitty litter.

344
00:27:00,500 --> 00:27:02,676
Everyone's lives are depending on me.

345
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:09,700
I have to destroy it.

346
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:12,620
If I don't, they'll all die.

347
00:27:13,560 --> 00:27:18,980
I can't fight as well as everyone else,
even if I train ten times as hard.

348
00:27:24,840 --> 00:27:26,537
So I train a hundred.

349
00:27:26,620 --> 00:27:28,700
Two hundred times harder!

350
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:33,220
There's something out there
worth protecting, right?

351
00:27:33,540 --> 00:27:35,080
So what is it?

352
00:27:36,980 --> 00:27:37,810
Kobe!

353
00:27:38,440 --> 00:27:39,440
It's too late!

354
00:27:39,620 --> 00:27:40,700
Abandon ship!

355
00:27:43,820 --> 00:27:45,640
You can save them

356
00:27:54,660 --> 00:27:59,660
I will stay in fact!

357
00:28:39,400 --> 00:28:41,060
What was that?

358
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:42,260
We're saved!

359
00:28:42,580 --> 00:28:43,640
No, not yet!

360
00:28:43,880 --> 00:28:45,292
There's too much debris!

361
00:28:48,680 --> 00:28:50,520
That's why I'm here!

362
00:28:50,820 --> 00:28:52,100
Off-web!

363
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:02,400
There you go!

364
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:06,380
Kobe!

365
00:29:07,240 --> 00:29:08,070
Hey!

366
00:29:10,660 --> 00:29:11,640
Kobe!

367
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,740
I don't even know what to say!

368
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:18,080
That hell no, Paul.

369
00:29:19,140 --> 00:29:19,980
I did it.

370
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:25,320
Yeah, you did, buddy.

371
00:29:25,860 --> 00:29:27,320
You were amazing.

372
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:29,820
Look at you.

373
00:29:30,220 --> 00:29:33,040
Strong enough to bring down a mountain.

374
00:29:37,420 --> 00:29:39,720
Let's go home, you maniac.

375
00:29:47,540 --> 00:29:50,000
Captain, help me out of my way!

376
00:29:50,540 --> 00:29:52,240
Welcome back, you two!

377
00:29:52,940 --> 00:29:54,058
Okay, you're alive!

378
00:29:56,780 --> 00:29:57,760
Hey, body.

379
00:29:59,300 --> 00:30:00,220
You're okay.

380
00:30:01,280 --> 00:30:03,140
We're all going home.

381
00:30:05,660 --> 00:30:08,460
Okay, once Garp is back, we'll take off.

382
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:14,070
Click.

383
00:30:14,600 --> 00:30:15,960
This is Garp.

384
00:30:16,480 --> 00:30:19,700
The mission to rescue
Captain Koei is a success.

385
00:30:20,820 --> 00:30:22,644
Vice Admiral, you're all right.

386
00:30:22,940 --> 00:30:25,234
Hurry back to the ship and we'll leave.

387
00:30:27,160 --> 00:30:31,260
Actually, depart from Fulalad
immediately. That's an order.

388
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:33,230
What?

389
00:30:33,860 --> 00:30:36,157
Vice Admiral, what are you talking about?

390
00:30:36,240 --> 00:30:38,400
Don't you worry about this, old man.

391
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:43,540
Our top priority in this mission is
the safety of everyone on that ship.

392
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:45,080
Am I wrong?

393
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:52,060
We can't go! Hurry!

394
00:30:52,280 --> 00:30:53,515
Turn the ship around!

395
00:30:54,500 --> 00:30:56,300
We've won the battle today!

396
00:30:57,040 --> 00:31:00,640
Our victory sends a
message to all pirates!

397
00:31:04,340 --> 00:31:06,817
Please, you have to let
me join the Marines!

398
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:09,977
I'll clean and scrub and do any
chores that you'd like me to!

399
00:31:10,060 --> 00:31:12,178
I'll do anything to become a Marine!

400
00:31:13,880 --> 00:31:16,620
What did you boys join
the Navy to protect?

401
00:31:18,740 --> 00:31:21,060
It's the future of all people, right?

402
00:31:21,480 --> 00:31:26,760
You'll be part of that future, for years
to come, long after the old man's gone.

403
00:31:27,860 --> 00:31:29,820
Take that baby and go.

404
00:31:31,140 --> 00:31:33,060
Live your lives.

405
00:31:51,020 --> 00:31:52,420
Keep going.

406
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:55,740
You all are the future of the Navy.

407
00:31:56,480 --> 00:31:58,040
Don't look back!

408
00:32:08,840 --> 00:32:10,377
What were you thinking?

409
00:32:10,460 --> 00:32:11,960
In the future,

410
00:32:12,100 --> 00:32:16,097
will you please limit the tasteless
lectures in front of the young recruits?

411
00:32:16,180 --> 00:32:17,240
Why should I?

412
00:32:17,380 --> 00:32:19,674
But young people's future is limitless!

413
00:32:31,840 --> 00:32:37,340
The next day, newspapers reported the
heroic rescue of the Navy's young hero,

414
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:38,470
Captain Koby,

415
00:32:38,553 --> 00:32:42,497
along with the sorrowful
news that Vice and Mulgarb

416
00:32:42,580 --> 00:32:45,300
disappeared after his
battle on Pirate Island.

417
00:32:45,720 --> 00:32:49,497
It was also reported that
the Emperor of the Sea Straw

418
00:32:49,580 --> 00:32:54,600
Hat Luffy had barricaded himself
on the future island, Egghead.
